THE METHOD THIS SOFTWARE IMPLEMENTS

The BeCoMe (Best-Compromise Mean) method is not the work of this author. Ivan Vrana,
Jan Tyrychtr and Martin Pelikan published it:

  Vrana, I., Tyrychtr, J., & Pelikan, M. (2021). BeCoMe: Easy-to-implement optimized
  method for best-compromise group decision making: Flood-prevention and COVID-19 case
  studies. Environmental Modelling & Software, 136, 104953.
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envsoft.2020.104953

Copyright covers expression, not ideas, so a published method carries no copyright that
this implementation could infringe. The licence above therefore applies to this source
code alone and makes no claim over the method itself, which remains free for anyone to
implement. What those authors are owed is citation, and this file gives it.


CASE-STUDY DATA AND REFERENCE VALUES

The three expert panels in examples/data/ (budget, floods, pendlers) and the expected
results in tests/reference/ originate from the method authors' own Excel workbook. This
repository reproduces them so the test suite can check its own results against theirs.
It matches to within 0.001 on every run. Credit for that data belongs to the method's
authors, not to this author.
